Technical difficulty: A prototype month-end expression raised numpy UFuncInputCastingError because month and day datetime units were mixed; explicit nanosecond cutoffs fixed it.
2026-08-02: Widened frozen posterior states with a 60-day organization/type/category view and raised product-residual activation to 0.995 confidence. This was chosen from four train-only monthly folds: the 60-day view scored 0.9896528, 0.9961248, 0.9915118, and 0.9963921 before further graph residuals, consistently ahead of the all-history view.
2026-08-02: Added train-only posterior-error weighting to the residual loss so the graph receives a measurable gradient from the rare hierarchy mistakes while retaining the high-support residual penalty.
2026-08-02: Added a 0.03-percentage-point forward-fold stability band for posterior/graph blend selection. The graph's measured January gain was only 0-2 rows depending on CUDA execution, so the simpler zero residual blend wins that statistical tie while the graph pipeline still trains and is available when a material fold gain exists.
2026-08-02: Confirmed the recent posterior on evaluation-shaped internal horizons: at a 2019-07 cutoff with a six-month query window, 60-day history plus the 0.995 product gate scored 0.9923751 versus 0.9919217 for all history; the earlier five-month fold differed by only 0.011 points in favor of all history.
2026-08-02: Applied deterministic 24-neighbor historical item fanout inside each relation state and a support-ranked 12-relation fanout in the second GraphSAGE layer, matching the requested [24,12] sampling budget without changing the separately frozen posterior.
